  "notes": "12-segment, 7-point elliptical lathe (120 triangles) + one 20-triangle head + six legs: 212 before the seven exact unions, 326 after them (1.09x the 300 budget, inside the spec 1.6x allowance), one closed shell.  Body 64 x 47 mm in plan by design (the lathe radius is scaled per angle by BODY_ASPECT 0.735), dome top at 55.5 mm, underside at 9-10 mm.  Legs run from (x, +-17 mm, 22 mm) inside the shell to feet at (x-4 mm, +-27.5 mm, 4.2 mm), section 10 mm tapering to 8.4 mm.  Dorsal seam: the columns at 0 and 180 degrees are pulled 8% in on every ring, which pinches a groove along y=0.  Materials after the union: |y| < 6 mm and z > 32 mm = brass (the seam), z < 12 mm or within 1.15 head radii of the head centre = rubber, the rest chitin.  fit_bounds pins 90 x 55 x 60 mm.",
